From 5501fa39f6426c2d3145099e9b6e0ea74e7bfd28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:11:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(effects): opt-in border effects on unfocused windows
 (#563)

Add `[effects] border_unfocused = false`: when true, the border effect
draws on every window passing the non-focus gates (decorated, calm,
not fullscreen) and on their overview cards, not just the focused one.
Default off keeps today's behavior bit-identical.

Gate widened via `BorderEffectGate::allowUnfocused`, filled at the two
producers (view ownGate, overview cardGate) so the predicate stays a
pure, unit-testable function of its struct.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
